        <body>
            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0741" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg647"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-29"><hi rendition="#italic">October 29, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Nov. 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 588.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reference to Department’s No. 517 of the
                    5th of June last, relative to the arrest on the coast of Cuba of the American
                    citizen, Bert S. Skiller, I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy, with
                    translation, of a note received from the minister of state upon the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d542-a1.xml" xpointer="d542-a1"/>
